WEBVTT

00:00:10.442 --> 00:00:13.875
<v><b>Emma:</b></v> I kind of think it’s been similar for a long time, hasn’t it,

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.954
the kind of texts that you have to study at school?

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:25.998
<v><b>Joanne:</b></v> So perhaps the more important thing is actually just to get children reading,…

00:00:32.171 --> 00:00:36.207
<v><b>Joanne:</b></v> Rather than what it is that they read. I mean, arguably, if the child is given Shakespeare…

00:00:41.848 --> 00:00:45.026
<v><b>Sean:</b></v> I think that’s the important thing; it’s all about when it’s introduced…

00:00:50.933 --> 00:00:55.744
<v><b>Sean:</b></v> …and I remember a, a turning point at about 16, thinking, hang on,

00:00:55.769 --> 00:00:56.999
this is actually quite interesting…

00:01:03.203 --> 00:01:08.071
<v><b>Sean:</b></v> …that’s the thing; if you don’t do it at school, when, when will you see the classics? Yeah.

00:01:14.127 --> 00:01:16.548
<v><b>Emma:</b></v> And I guess it’s how it’s taught to you as well.